; **This run ends in the north pier, not at the gap's edge.** It used to run
; z -19.4..2.0 and carry the whole of the east wall's middle; the gate takes
; z -5.0..1.0 out of it, and the run stops at -9.0 so its end is buried half a
; metre inside the pier that closes it. That is the west arch's arrangement
; exactly — see `perim_w_arch_n`, which stops at -9.0 against `arch_pier_north`
; for the same reason: a wall that stops *on* the reveal leaves a joint at the
; one place the eye is aimed, and a wall that stops inside the pier leaves none.
[node name="perim_e_mid_n" type="CSGBox3D" parent="."]
