; The east gate: the seventh way out, and the only one that faces another.
;
; It is on the fountain's own east-west line, which is the whole reason for
; cutting a new opening rather than using the `ne` or `se` threshold already in
; this wall. Those sit at 62 and 121 degrees, and a monument behind either is a
; monument you come across; due east of the fountain it is the west arch's
; answer, and the plaza reads as a notch between the two of them. Turn west from
; the coping and the ground falls six metres; turn east and it climbs six.
;
; **Mirrored in arrangement and not in coordinate.** The plaza is not symmetric —
; the west wall stands at x -38.5 with faces at -33 and -44, the east at 41.5
; with faces at 36 and 47 — so copying the arch's numbers with the sign flipped
; would have put these piers three metres adrift of their own wall. What is
; mirrored is the *arrangement*: piers the full depth of the wall plus 2.5m
; proud of its inner face, a 6m opening between them, the walls either side
; ending half a metre inside the piers, and a beam at the near plane. Every one
; of those is measured off the east wall's own faces. `ParkPlan.EAST_GAP_AT`,
; `EAST_GAP_MOUTH_X` and `EAST_GAP_FAR_X` are the same numbers written down for
; the generators, and `_east_gate` asserts this scene against them.
[node name="east_pier_north" type="CSGBox3D" parent="."]
