; The beam, and it is what the arch's is: a header bearing on both piers rather
; than a slab of wall left floating. Set in the front 0.9m of the passage with
; its plaza face flush on the piers', lapping 2.2m onto each.
;
; **6.30 to 7.40, and the soffit is the arch's exactly.** Equal by choice rather
; than by derivation — the two gates face each other across 80m of plaza and a
; player at the fountain sees both at once, so a centimetre of difference would
; be invisible and a metre would be a mistake nobody could name.
;
; What it crops is not the arch's problem in reverse. West, the soffit had to
; clear the wheel's rim and very nearly did not; east, it deliberately cuts the
; rim's crest off — from `ParkPlan.EAST_NEAR_STAND_X` the ray reaches 29m by the
; time it gets to the ridge, which stands at 50. That is not the wheel's mistake
; repeated: the wheel was visible *only* through the arch, so cropping it lost
; the thing entirely, and the ridge stands over the whole east roofline from
; anywhere in the plaza. The gap shows its foot and the cascade; the skyline
; shows its head.
;
; Collides, because it is 6.3m up over a route the player walks.
[node name="east_beam" type="CSGBox3D" parent="."]
