; The arch is a cutting, and the three boxes below are the whole of it: two piers
; and a beam across their faces.
;
; It was 9m wide, 8.9m clear and 11m deep — a section nearly square, which is a
; hole in a wall rather than a passage. So on 2026-08-14 it became a tube: 6 by 5
; over 13.5m, the depth got by projecting the piers 2.5m *into* the plaza rather
; than thickening the wall, because the wall's west face is the terrace's east
; edge and the terrace has only six metres to give.
;
; **The top came off on 2026-08-16, and the depth stayed.** The tube's own lintel
; was the thing cropping the west view, and it was cropping it in the one
; direction nobody had measured. A soffit at 5m over 13.5m of depth is not a 5m
; ceiling — the *far* edge is what limits, and from the ring's west vertex that
; edge sits 28m off, which puts the ceiling on a 6.7° ray. The wheel's crown is
; `ParkPlan.WHEEL_TOP`, 25.80, and it stands 87m off from that same vertex: the
; ray reaches y=12 by the time it gets there, which is a hand under the hub — so
; rather more than the top half of the section's biggest silhouette was behind
; masonry from everywhere in the plaza.
;
; **That height read 21.9 here until 2026-08-16b and it was wrong by 3.9m**, the
; last of the four places carrying a figure reconstructed from `SHORE_TOP` plus
; two radii rather than read out of `west_far.tscn`. `CLAUDE.md`, `ParkPlan` and
; `west_capture.gd` were corrected the day it was found and this file was missed,
; which is the failure mode a fifth survey exists to produce: the *argument* here
; was sound at 21.9 and is stronger at 25.8, so nothing looked wrong. Read
; `WHEEL_TOP`; do not add anything up.
;
; Lateral was never the problem and the arithmetic below is still true —
; the pavilion and the pier fit inside the 6m slot whole, from every standpoint,
; and did under the 9m arch too. Height was the whole of it.
;
; So: two piers, 6m apart and 13.5m deep, cut clean through the wall to the sky,
; with a beam across their plaza faces at 6.30 to carry the sign. The beam is at
; the *near* plane, which is why it costs almost nothing — from the fountain rim
; it is 18.5m off against the old far edge's 32, so the same 6.3m head clears the
; wheel by four metres where 5m at the far edge missed it by ten.
;
; What is given up is the tube. The approach still narrows — 104m of plaza, an 8m
; forecourt, a 6m slot — but it narrows in plan only, and the section swap that
; happens inside it no longer has a roof to hide under. It does not need one:
; `_hold_shot` cuts to a fixed camera and walks the player out of frame, which
; has been the actual cover since the seam moved here.
;
; The through-view, unchanged and still what the overlook depends on: the arch
; frames the gap in the boardwalk's frontage and the gap frames the pier. From
; the fountain the near mouth is 29m off and the far one 44m, so on the axis the
; near opening projects 4.5m either side at the far plane — wider than the far
; opening's own 3m. The whole of the far end is still in view.
[node name="arch_pier_north" type="CSGBox3D" parent="."]
