; The beam, which is what is left of the mass over the opening and the only part
; of it that was ever doing a job the view could afford.
;
; Set in the front 0.9m of the cutting with its west face flush on the piers'
; plaza faces, so it reads as a header bearing on both rather than as a slab of
; wall left floating. It laps 2.2m onto each pier for the same reason — a beam
; that stops at the reveal has nothing to sit on.
;
; 6.30 to 7.40. The soffit is set by the wheel and not by taste: it has to clear
; `ParkPlan.WHEEL_TOP` — 25.80, read and not reconstructed — at 87m from the
; furthest anyone stands on the axis, which is the ring's west vertex at −16 with
; the fountain blocking everything behind it.
;
; **What 6.30 buys is a range and not a number, so it is quoted as one.** The
; camera is not at the standpoint: the spring arm hangs it about 2.5m back, and
; its height moves with the shot's pitch — 1.10 to 1.47 measured in the running
; game across the west poses. Over that range this soffit puts the ceiling at the
; wheel's distance between **26.9m and 28.5m** (both computed, at the two
; measured eye heights), against a crown at 25.80. It clears at either end.
;
; `ParkPlan.ARCH_HEIGHT` carries the number and the standpoint table with it.
; Do not restate the required-soffit figures here — a fifth copy of them is how
; the 21.9 above survived three corrections.
;
; Collides, because it is 6.3m up over a route the player walks and the boardwalk
; copy of it in `_plaza_from_below` is two metres from where they arrive.
[node name="arch_beam" type="CSGBox3D" parent="."]
