; The parapet, in two runs with a five-metre gap between them **on the arch's
; own axis since 2026-08-14**.
;
; The gap used to be 2.6m at the terrace's north end, because it was the mouth of
; a slot cut in the bluff and the stair inside it was 2.6m wide. That put the way
; down off to one side of a route that arrives dead centre, and put an unbroken
; rail straight ahead of the arch — so the overlook showed you the boardwalk and
; nothing at all about how to reach it.
;
; On the axis it is the opposite: you walk out of the tunnel and the way down is
; the thing in front of you, with the view over the rail either side of it. The
; walk west becomes one straight line from the ring to the head of the flight.
[node name="overlook_parapet_s" type="CSGBox3D" parent="."]
