; **Two runs since the east gate was cut, and the gap between them is the gate's
; own.** This is the plaza's outer boundary — the 3.6m wall at the edge of the
; 104m slab that stops the player walking off it — and it ran unbroken past the
; new opening, so the gate was a doorway onto a wall four metres further on. The
; walk test found it and nothing else could have: from inside the plaza the gate
; frames the monument perfectly well over the top of a 3.6m wall.
;
; The gap is z -14..9, which is the west's exactly. There it is 23m because the
; terrace past the arch is walked along; here it is 23m because that is the width
; of the monument the court is in front of — the wings reach -14.3 to 10.3 — so
; the same number lands for a different reason, which is worth knowing if either
; one moves.
[node name="wall_east_mid_n" type="CSGBox3D" parent="."]
