; The fountain. It was five CSG cylinders written out above this line until
; 2026-08-14c — a base, a bowl, a plinth, a shaft and a finial, which is a
; wedding cake with no water in it. It is now 270-odd parts and two shaders, and
; that is far past what belongs hand-typed in a scene file.
;
; It leaves `plaza.tscn` rather than growing inside it because of what this file
; is *for*. The perimeter is hand-laid because it is a room shape being
; designed, and `plaza_frontage.tscn` reads its runs back out of this text. The
; fountain is not a room shape, it is an assembly, and every other assembly in
; the park is generated output. What stays here is the ground, the walls and the
; tower — the plaza itself, rather than the things standing in it.
[node name="fountain" parent="." instance=ExtResource("14_fountain")]

; What the perimeter is made of. Generated output of `tools/gen_props.gd`, which
; reads the `perim_*` runs out of this very file and lays the frontage against
; them — so moving a wall here moves its shopfronts on the next generator run,
; and nothing has to be kept in step by hand.
[node name="frontage" parent="." instance=ExtResource("13_frontage")]

